{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done","id":1535657,"title":"What's the worst act that your character done?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-15T11:55:03-07:00","id":1535657,"title":"What's the worst act that your character done?","content":"I'm curious to what you done in your games that stand out as a horrible act by your kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T14:12:36-07:00","id":1535674,"title":"","content":"Tbh I'm pretty bad at being bad as a player.<br /> <br /> My worse action was to use Vicissitude on a Garou to turn him into a backpack, his agony heightened by the constant need to remold his form, then lock him in a silver cage and forcibly Ghoul him.<br /> <br /> All pretty evil, except my character was just trying to ensure survival for both. He was found staked by the Sabbat and introduced to them without proper brainwashing, was just following orders until he could escape, and feigned utter evil to justify not killing the defeated werewolf.<br /> <br /> Even the Ghouling was just so the Garou wouldn't kill him first thing after freed. And free him I did. The character was clueless about what it really entails for the Silver Fangs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  It was unfinished, posted by accident 05-15-2024, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T08:18:47-07:00","id":1535732,"title":"","content":"I once instigated a pogrom which purged all venetians in a Greek city to hurt clan giovanni. Hundreds died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T12:17:56-07:00","id":1535744,"title":"","content":"Horrible is a simple term, but what makes one act more or less horrible is highly subjective.<br /> <br /> I had a Giovanni who was business focused, property ownership, business take overs, etc. One branch of his business was a human trafficking group specializing in children. Once the kids were &quot;retirement age&quot; of 12+ and were too mentally and emotionally broken, the Giovanni would sell them to Nagaraja as food or necromancy components. All in all it was a win/win/win, the Giovanni got multiple returns on investment, the Nagaraja get fed, and the kids get put out of their misery. This also secured a limited form of Necromantic knowledge trade.<br /> <br /> In a different game I had Follower of Set who turned the mortal daughter of a rival Ventrue into a ghoul warrior hell bent on exterminating her fathers bloodline. This was an ancient setting game, the Ventrue had earned his embrace during the 2nd Punic war. Two millennia later she was still butchering mortals descended from their family line, if anything the modern invention of genetic heritage companies like &quot;23 and me&quot; just gave her a longer kill list. And all of this was over the fact that the Follower of Set had lost a trade deal when Carthage fell.<br /> <br /> In a third game, we ran an all Assamite coterie with members specializing in different methods of death. My character was a sniper with knowledge of explosives, which meant the ST had a habit of trying to force face to face combat. This culminated in a game where our target was a high ranking Garou who ran the local werewolf pack. Rather than trying to fight them directly my sniper simply targeted the local kinfolk and would take out any pack member who was trying to protect them. After a month of this all the kinfolk were dead and most of the pack had either been killed or driven off. Eventually the pack leader went mad with grief and impotent rage, allowing for a much easier kill shot.<br /> <br /> So which one is the most horrible to your sensibilities? The kids who my character never directly interacted with, the vengeful ghoul who all I did was provide a story and some support to, or the sniper who personally butchered an entire community just to drive his true target out into the open?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T13:26:54-07:00","id":1535748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done?p=1535744#post1535744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So which one is the most horrible to your sensibilities? The kids who my character never directly interacted with, the vengeful ghoul who all I did was provide a story and some support to, or the sniper who personally butchered an entire community just to drive his true target out into the open?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, the worst is Giovanni.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T16:18:31-07:00","id":1535754,"title":"","content":"Well, my Tremere in Transylvania Chronicles...<br /> <br /> ...had an ongoing deal with Vykos (who was his one <i>ally</i> at the start of the chronicle, due to having known each other as mortal mages) to whack his Tzimisce rivals in exchange for him whacking my Tremere's rivals, sharing information and just committing general treason all over the place, because fuck each other's clans but especially the Tremere.<br /> <br /> ...feeding the coterie's Gangrel a nonstop supply of gargoyles for about a century, mostly because it amused my Tremere to see what creative means he'd come up with to do it. Finally told the Gangrel to knock it off when the clan started getting suspicious as to why he needed a new gargoyle every few years.<br /> <br /> ...performed a backyard abortion as part of an improvised ritual to appease Kupala (at least temporarily) during the 1314 story. It <i>kinda</i> worked.<br /> <br /> ...had about <i>this</i> reaction to Dracula's &quot;hundred orphans&quot; stunt:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sBffNiUOeiA\" data-code=\"sBffNiUOeiA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sBffNiUOeiA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> ...koldun genocide. Want to learn koldunism to openly mock the Tzimisce, but can't do it the easy way? Just diablerize enough to piece together memories of how to perform the correct pacts, and learn ways and rituals yourself.<br /> <br /> ...the following exchange:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Me: </i>&quot;I tell my apprentice to do as I say, or I'm going to kill him.&quot;<br /> <i>ST:</i> &quot;Roll intimidation.&quot;<br /> <i>Me:</i> &quot;I'm not trying to intimidate him, I'm telling him flat out what the consequences of refusing to follow my orders will be. It's his choice.&quot;<br /> <i>ST:</i> &quot;Well he refuses, he thinks you're bluffing.&quot;<br /> <i>Me: </i>&quot;I hit him with LotF level 5. Six successes on my Willpower roll.&quot;<br /> <i>ST: </i>&quot;Shit, well, okay...he frenzies, runs away screaming, and dies.&quot;<br /> <i>Me: </i>&quot;I go to my next apprentice and tell him to do what the first was going to do, or I'm going to kill him.&quot;<br /> <i>ST:</i> &quot;You don't have to tell him, he's already on it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>...then there was the <i>minor</i> case of mortal genocide, murdering almost the entirety of Transylvania's Saxon population (and destroying every Tremere chantry in Transylvania, except Ceoris for obvious reasons) in the course of about a week. It wasn't so much about the genocide as it was making a statement to the Tremere -- the genocide was more or less my Tremere's resignation letter and announcement he was joining Goratrix in exile. Got my Tremere on the Red List, but I got around it with even more planning than the genocide itself entailed.<br /> <br /> ...cat eugenics. That really speaks for itself, but while my Tremere was laying low from having being put on the Red List, he got bored and spent a century or so learning Biothaumaturgy and adapting Sculpt the Perfect Servant for animals. Use the ritual on a pregnant cat, pick the best of the litter, use Biothaumaturgy on them to jack their attributes into the stratosphere while being able to do things like speak, breed them, wash, rinse, repeat.<br /> <br /> The cat ghoul my Tremere ended up with was one unholy terror. The only PC with higher mental attributes was my Tremere, and that cat was pretty close to him. The little fucker figured out how to circumvent my Tremere's ritual protections over his library, had been raiding it while my Tremere was daysleeping, and <i>learned thaumaturgy</i>. My Tremere found it funny and endearing his little cat ran around around hunting mice by setting them on fire...until the night it managed to kill an entire Sabbat pack on its own, because somehow, some way, it managed to learn Thaumaturgy <i>3</i>.<br /> <br /> Then it got <i>hilarious</i>. My Tremere even made him his own little purple silk collar with mirrored name tag, as foci for Pavise of Fouled Presence and Incorporeal Passage.<br /> <br /> ...<i>people</i> eugenics. The cat experiment turned out so well, my Tremere replicated it with humans. Didn't work out nearly as well as the cat, but his ghouls could give neonate Brujah a run for their money at least. Went to great effort to ensure the human ghouls never learned Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> ...hunting and slaughtering entire packs of lupines (and Sabbat), to reduce them down to principal foci because. My Tremere had diablerized so much from his koldunism stunt, he developed methuselah's thirst by the age of 500. Werewolves were just the easiest snacks to find and cover up the deed.<br /> <br /> ...partnering with the Setite and Lasombra PC to get into the darksteel trade. My Tremere was a hella necromancer, atop everything else. The Setite would do his thing to make sure the mortals were primed and ready to pass on as the best-quality&quot; ore&quot;, the Lasombra would make them pass only as Lasombra can (making sure they were nice and exposed to Oblivion in the process), my characters' spirit slaves would forge them. The favors we got in return went towards empowering the Setite's and Lasombra's skinlands holdings, making for a nice little growth model. At the time the chronicle ended, my Tremere had damn near cornered the market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T16:58:18-07:00","id":1535755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done?p=1535744#post1535744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horrible is a simple term, but what makes one act more or less horrible is highly subjective.<br /> <br /> I had a Giovanni who was business focused, property ownership, business take overs, etc. One branch of his business was a human trafficking group specializing in children. Once the kids were &quot;retirement age&quot; of 12+ and were too mentally and emotionally broken, the Giovanni would sell them to Nagaraja as food or necromancy components. All in all it was a win/win/win, the Giovanni got multiple returns on investment, the Nagaraja get fed, and the kids get put out of their misery. This also secured a limited form of Necromantic knowledge trade.<br /> <br /> In a different game I had Follower of Set who turned the mortal daughter of a rival Ventrue into a ghoul warrior hell bent on exterminating her fathers bloodline. This was an ancient setting game, the Ventrue had earned his embrace during the 2nd Punic war. Two millennia later she was still butchering mortals descended from their family line, if anything the modern invention of genetic heritage companies like &quot;23 and me&quot; just gave her a longer kill list. And all of this was over the fact that the Follower of Set had lost a trade deal when Carthage fell.<br /> <br /> In a third game, we ran an all Assamite coterie with members specializing in different methods of death. My character was a sniper with knowledge of explosives, which meant the ST had a habit of trying to force face to face combat. This culminated in a game where our target was a high ranking Garou who ran the local werewolf pack. Rather than trying to fight them directly my sniper simply targeted the local kinfolk and would take out any pack member who was trying to protect them. After a month of this all the kinfolk were dead and most of the pack had either been killed or driven off. Eventually the pack leader went mad with grief and impotent rage, allowing for a much easier kill shot.<br /> <br /> So which one is the most horrible to your sensibilities? The kids who my character never directly interacted with, the vengeful ghoul who all I did was provide a story and some support to, or the sniper who personally butchered an entire community just to drive his true target out into the open?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For most people? The Giovanni. In every scenario innocent people die, but in the first the get victims are children specifically, who get abused (I am assuming sexually) to the breaking point before the murder, that is likely to be extremely painful considering the Nagaraja feeding procedures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T10:54:02-07:00","id":1535776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done?p=1535755#post1535755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most people? The Giovanni. In every scenario innocent people die, but in the first the get victims are children specifically, who get abused (I am assuming sexually) to the breaking point before the murder, that is likely to be extremely painful considering the Nagaraja feeding procedures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the Nagaraja get retconned to not produce the effects of the kiss when they bite? I remember there was some debate over what happens when a Nagaraja &quot;licks&quot; a feeding wound, does the skin heal over the empty crater of flesh that was just consumed.<br /> <br /> The Gentleman Gamer had an interesting video way back in the mists of time describing the concept of a Nagaraja who had a Herd which functioned like a cult, with each member offering up parts of themselves, but that only really works if you have a way to staunch the bleeding from the tissue loss.<br /> <br /> As far a Nagarja feeding from a child it gets particularly insidious when you consider that since Dominate is a clan discipline, they can rework the child's memory however they wish. Making the traumas better or worse, or making the child think that they owe the Nagaraja for saving them and thus they need to feed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T09:18:46-07:00","id":1535992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done?p=1535754#post1535754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my Tremere in Transylvania Chronicles...<br /> <br /> ...hunting and slaughtering entire packs of lupines (and Sabbat), to reduce them down to principal foci because. My Tremere had diablerized so much from his koldunism stunt, he developed methuselah's thirst by the age of 500. Werewolves were just the easiest snacks to find and cover up the deed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems counter productive, IF you are strong enough to hunt packs of lupines, you are strong enough to capture some, or even better, Dominate the whole bunch, to get a self replenishing blood supply. The 80%-90% blood loss is nothing to a Werewolf regeneration, but death is pretty damn permanent and causes a lot of other problems.<br /> <br /> It sounds you had a blast of a game, but it is not verosimile everything reads like a power fantasy, but good for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-20T19:28:27-07:00","id":1536026,"title":"","content":"Killed a young lady's baby-daddy/pimp, in front of her, then, used his blood to teach her Wyrm-lore; by the time the night was over, she had one dot in Wyrm-Lore. (It was in a vampire-game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T04:11:55-07:00","id":1536050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done?p=1535992#post1535992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds you had a blast of a game, but it is not verosimile everything reads like a power fantasy, but good for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Transylvania Chronicles and I was playing Tremere. Trust me when I say most of that wasn't power fantasy but rather survival strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T04:56:36-07:00","id":1536051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535657-what-s-the-worst-act-that-your-character-done#post1535657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to what you done in your games that stand out as a horrible act by your kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we include NPCs...<br /> Ventrue elder<br /> He incited the genocide of a cultural minority to long-term destabilize a region and create a threat/conflict that justified radical policies by his meat puppets in the government, while at the same time filling his coffers from contracts with the arms and oil industries. You need to re-kindle this setup every ten years or so, but all you do is 'lobbying'.<br /> <br /> Totally fictional concept that certainly wasn't inspired by any real events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-catego